<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22970" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ēbrĭo</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. a.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make
			drunk</i>, <i>inebriate</i> (<b>poet.</b> and post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palma vescentes inebriat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 22, 47, § 103</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. 14, 1, 3, § 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				83, 27</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of colors, <i>to
				saturate'</i> amethystum inebriatur Tyrio, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 41,
				65, § 139</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Of plants: inebriatae radices, i. q. nimis
					irrigatae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 26, 40, § 247</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurem,</span>”
				<i>to fill full of talk</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					9, 113</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
